<Project>

  <!--
    Stops NuGet Central Package Management from leaking into vendored
    third-party trees (upstream declares its own PackageReference versions).

    NuGet imports the NEAREST Directory.Packages.props walking up from the
    project directory, and imports only that one. Because this file declares
    no <ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>, the vendored tree is outside CPM:
    the root's Directory.Packages.props never reaches it.

    RULE FOR ANY FUTURE VENDORED TREE
    ---------------------------------
    This file belongs with contrib/external/Directory.Build.props and
    contrib/external/Directory.Build.targets, one directory level above the
    vendored tree's root. All three travel together; a vendored tree with
    only one of them inherits half of the root's build policy.
  -->

</Project>
